48.What happens to our data when a docker container exits? 
Container data is temporary by default; to persist data even after removing the container, we use Docker volumes or bind mounts.
49.What are docker objects?
Docker objects are the resources that Docker manages.
The main Docker objects are Images, Containers, Networks, and Volumes.
Docker also manages objects such as Services and Secrets in Docker Swarm.

